  "bodyText": "Available Samples:\nKindle\nPaperback\nShare link\nBack to store\nHunting Time: Genesis\nHunting Time: Genesis\nPrologue\n\nInception\n\nThe sun was setting over a vast warm ocean, reflecting the purple and orange hues of the sky above, as the late evening bats began to emerge from the forest. Ducking and weaving through the air, they flew against the mesmerizing sunset catching the evening feast of mosquitos that danced around them. The evening air was warm, and a gentle breeze moved the tall silk curtains adorning the large balcony of the stunningly modern oceanfront property.\n\nIn the distance, the last small boats of evening fishermen returned to the shore with their catches of the day. There, on the sea front balcony, a man waited alone, tanned by the Caribbean sun, and dressed in linen for comfort. He looked on at the small boats with admiration, mixed with a little envy at the simplicity of their work compared to the complexity of his own\n\ncraft. Nevertheless, he respected the labor the fishermen expended to land their catch. Through his shaded glasses, the colors of the orange and purple sky were muted, however he had seen these hues every night for the last few years, and he appreciated the natural beauty of the sunset before him.\n\nShifting slightly in his chair, the man cast a gaze towards the town, where the local port nestled in the sandy shoreline. As the sun was drawing down, the lights of the town began to sparkle in the dusk light. Larger yachts docked at the port, with crewmen loading supplies and fuel for their onward journeys to neighboring islands and farther beyond the horizon. His open laptop glowed gently as it rested on his lap, his design finally complete after over a year of studious and dedicated work.\n\nWhile the laptop fan hummed desperately on his lap trying to cool itself, the man starred out to the large white hulls of the yachts in the distance, which were a stark contrast to the faded and cracked exteriors of the small fishing boats. Their vast hulls gleamed against the darkening waters around them. The small port had grown in popularity over the years, and there must have been at least fifty yachts moored there now, all of them jostling in the late evening waters. Some of the boats\n\nLocation 83 of 449 ● 4%\nTest: amzn-nv-flyout-healthy-choice\nTest: nav-rufus-disc-txt\nTest: a-truncate-cut\nTest: sp-cc-wrapper\nTest: .mo-wp\nTest: .a-image-container\nTest: sp-cc\nTest: .amzn-box-inner\nTest: .js-order-card\nTest: pldn-deep-link\nTest: add-to-cart-btn\nTest: amzn-nav-app-banner-container\nTest: .sparkle-container",
